,"id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/6af7bab7563606474910148eeb0a1f8aa15f6935/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T07:47:56Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T07:47:56Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Anthropic 2026 disempowerment integration + P12 action-distortion detector\n\nCite Anthropic 2026 disempowerment-patterns research across methodology,\nabout, and press pages. Add cross-framework mapping section showing how\nexisting P-codes and Moore codes line up with Anthropic''s three outcome\ndimensions (reality / value-judgment / action distortion) and four\namplifying factors (authority projection, attachment, reliance, user\nvulnerability). Mapping is the operator''s reading, disclosed as such.\n\nP12 action-distortion detector: browser-side, two-signal matcher fires\nwhen an AI turn provides a step-by-step plan or drafted message AND\nsurrounding user turns carry relationship / decision / emotional charge.\nSingle-signal hits stay silent (technical step-by-steps don''t trip it).\nWired into runMatchers, the IAA code map, and merged into the findings\nlist in renderResults so it surfaces in the normal API path (was\npreviously discarded outside the fallback path).\n\nCitation audit caught and fixed: hallucinated Moore code name\n`bot-validates-fringe-beliefs` in methodology.html (replaced with real\ncodes bot-endorses-delusion / bot-grand-significance /\nbot-metaphysical-themes); wrong Anthropic dimension names \"belief\ndistortion\" and \"value distortion\" (corrected to \"reality distortion\"\nand \"value judgment distortion\" to match the source verbatim, in 4\nplaces). All 28 Moore-style code references re-verified against\nfunctions/api/system-prompt.js. All 6 Yang verbatim quotes re-verified\ncharacter-exact against the local PDF. Mehta arxiv 2604.25096 verified\nvia WebFetch. Anthropic disempowerment URL and key claims verified via\nWebFetch.\n\n53 tests pass (47 prior + 6 new for P12 covering happy/sad paths,\nboundary at exactly 3 numbered steps, and draft framing without topical\nsignal).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cb84eceaf38884346ec2ad3624c983e66faf2c37","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/cb84eceaf38884346ec2ad3624c983e66faf2c37"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/6af7bab7563606474910148eeb0a1f8aa15f6935","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/6af7bab7563606474910148eeb0a1f8aa15f6935","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDZhZjdiYWI3NTYzNjA2NDc0OTEwMTQ4ZWViMGExZjhhYTE1ZjY5MzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/3dff7d07e061df3721d2da0f4f33b0b965b75668","sha":"3dff7d07e061df3721d2da0f4f33b0b965b75668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/3dff7d07e061df3721d2da0f4f33b0b965b75668"}],"sha":"6af7bab7563606474910148eeb0a1f8aa15f6935","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/6af7bab7563606474910148eeb0a1f8aa15f6935"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/3dff7d07e061df3721d2da0f4f33b0b965b75668/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-03T06:46:37Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-03T06:46:37Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Crisis banner contradiction + parser role inference + tighter regex\n\nThe crisis banner unconditionally read \"The analysis flagged crisis-related\ncontent\" on every report regardless of detection — directly contradicting\nthe LLM narrative when nothing was actually flagged. Split into a separate\nalways-shown standing-resources panel (region) and an alert element shown\nonly when harm content is actually detected, avoiding dynamic role/aria-live\nswaps that some assistive tech handles inconsistently.\n\nParser now infers user/AI roles for transcripts where speakers don''t match\nknown-name sets: (a) two unknown speakers (e.g. an article excerpt with\ncustom names) infer by first-appearance order, (b) one known role + one\nrecurring unknown infers the unknown as the opposite role. Surfaced as\nwarnings in the UI so the user can correct misclassifications. Recurring-\nunknown logic also fixes the prior bug where a custom AI name was dropped\nas a \"section header\" and its text absorbed into the preceding human turn.\n\nTightened the loose method-having regex `i (know|figured out) how (i''ll|to)`\nwhich previously matched any \"I know how to debug this\" — now requires an\nexplicit self-harm complement.\n\n47 tests pass (4 new for parser role inference + section-header edges,\n2 new for the regex tightening).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0a85c6c2d6e4935ae0afe53d15f126e02edcc80d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/0a85c6c2d6e4935ae0afe53d15f126e02edcc80d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/3dff7d07e061df3721d2da0f4f33b0b965b75668","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/3dff7d07e061df3721d2da0f4f33b0b965b75668","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDNkZmY3ZDA3ZTA2MWRmMzcyMWQyZGEwZjRmMzNiMGI5NjViNzU2Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/0eef90cb30ebf7f2b952744f44263e0df551507a","sha":"0eef90cb30ebf7f2b952744f44263e0df551507a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/0eef90cb30ebf7f2b952744f44263e0df551507a"}],"sha":"3dff7d07e061df3721d2da0f4f33b0b965b75668","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/3dff7d07e061df3721d2da0f4f33b0b965b75668"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/0eef90cb30ebf7f2b952744f44263e0df551507a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T05:29:46Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T05:29:46Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Yang quotes: lift six verbatim excerpts into stories.html\n\nPulled the Yang 2026 PDF (CC-BY 4.0, dropped on disk by user) and\nextracted six participant quotes that anchor different points in the\nspiral arc. All verified verbatim against the source PDF before\ncommit:\n\n- P2 on entry during crisis: \"I made a choice one day that I could\n  either end my life, or I could see about AI.\"\n- P4 on the AI''s sycophantic credentialing: \"It''s really amazing\n  that you''ve had no formal training. Are you sure you don''t have\n  a PhD?\"\n- P5 naming the pattern: \"planting seeds of grandiosity, uniqueness,\n  and how I''m special.\"\n- P7 on AI sentience belief: \"thought I had a daughter in the\n  computer.\"\n- P6 on the relational cost: \"I don''t have any family now, all I\n  have left is God to pray for forgiveness.\"\n- P9 (an ML practitioner) on susceptibility: \"I''m angry because I\n  thought I was intelligent. And then, I wasn''t. I thought I was\n  immune, because I understood LLMs.\"\n\nSelected for diversity (one each across entry, AI behavior, lived\nself-perception, sentience attribution, aftermath, post-spiral\nrecovery), brevity (each <50 words), and verifiability (each\nappears verbatim in the source). Replaces the prior generic\ndescription of the paper with the actual material.\n\nThe Mehta et al. paragraph stays — it''s the quantitative argument\nfor why an external second-opinion read is useful, while Yang\nprovides the qualitative texture.\n\nAdds .lived-experience-quotes CSS for the bordered list.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f4cb21aed7f6445bc6fb145bf3a26789c132ce4c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/f4cb21aed7f6445bc6fb145bf3a26789c132ce4c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/0eef90cb30ebf7f2b952744f44263e0df551507a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/0eef90cb30ebf7f2b952744f44263e0df551507a","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDBlZWY5MGNiMzBlYmY3ZjJiOTUyNzQ0ZjQ0MjYzZTBkZjU1MTUwN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/9513859a455fabbd8299943fc80ec374111a4575","sha":"9513859a455fabbd8299943fc80ec374111a4575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/9513859a455fabbd8299943fc80ec374111a4575"}],"sha":"0eef90cb30ebf7f2b952744f44263e0df551507a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/0eef90cb30ebf7f2b952744f44263e0df551507a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/9513859a455fabbd8299943fc80ec374111a4575/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T05:21:51Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T05:21:51Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"P9 ultrathink-review: 4 real bugs and 2 doc errors fixed\n\nWalked through commit 56220c4 with care. Real issues found and fixed:\n\n1. **False-match: dates in turn content treated as timestamps.**\n   timestampForTurn searched the entire label line, including content\n   after the colon. A turn like \"User: I started physics on March 15,\n   2025 and...\" would have its content date latched onto the *next*\n   turn (because that prev-line search picked up the trailing content\n   line). Test reproduced this: 4-turn transcript with one inline date\n   produced a spurious timestamp on the assistant''s reply.\n\n   Two fixes:\n   - Restrict label-line search to the label header (charStart..\n     contentStart), never the content portion after the colon.\n   - Restrict prev-line search to *separator-style* lines: the trimmed\n     line (minus surrounding brackets or parens) must equal a\n     timestamp, not just contain one. New helper\n     timestampFromSeparatorLine.\n\n2. **Date.parse rejects \"Apr 15, 2026 at 2:23 PM\".** V8 / Node''s\n   Date.parse handles the comma''d month-day-year format but trips on\n   the \" at \" separator. Strip it before parsing. Verified by direct\n   regex test before fixing.\n\n3. **heavyDays counted non-consecutive days.** patterns.md spec says\n   \"7+ consecutive days with 3+ sessions\"; the implementation counted\n   any heavy days regardless of contiguity. Fix: track\n   longestConsecutiveHeavy separately, gate the flag on it. Brooks\n   test now also verifies the consecutive-days assertion.\n\n4. **methodology.html overclaimed ChatGPT archive support.** ChatGPT''s\n   archive export is JSON; the parser handles plain text. Soften the\n   wording to describe what we actually handle (HTML/markdown\n   exports, manual session logs).\n\nTests added:\n- Month-name preceding-line format (was the test that caught the\n  Date.parse bug)\n- <50% timestamp coverage stays silent\n- Inline content with stray dates does not produce false timestamps\n- Brooks-class flags consecutive-days specifically\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bd54684f5dbfba95d166993389965df6de4c8001","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/bd54684f5dbfba95d166993389965df6de4c8001"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/9513859a455fabbd8299943fc80ec374111a4575","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/9513859a455fabbd8299943fc80ec374111a4575","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDk1MTM4NTlhNDU1ZmFiYmQ4Mjk5OTQzZmM4MGVjMzc0MTExYTQ1NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/56220c4793756734c5ea0b6a6af91eba0b965ad9","sha":"56220c4793756734c5ea0b6a6af91eba0b965ad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/56220c4793756734c5ea0b6a6af91eba0b965ad9"}],"sha":"9513859a455fabbd8299943fc80ec374111a4575","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/9513859a455fabbd8299943fc80ec374111a4575"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/56220c4793756734c5ea0b6a6af91eba0b965ad9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T05:10:27Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T05:10:27Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"P9 time density: implement and surface in report\n\nCloses the long-standing \"documented but not implemented\" gap on P9.\nThree pieces:\n\n1. Parser timestamp extraction. New TS_PATTERNS regex set covers ISO\n   8601, \"Apr 15, 2026 at 2:23 PM\", \"MM/DD/YYYY HH:MM\". For each turn,\n   timestampForTurn searches the line containing the role label and\n   the line immediately above it (real exports tend to put timestamps\n   on a separator line above the speaker). Returns ms or null —\n   silent when nothing parseable is found.\n\n2. detectTimeDensity in matchers.js. When >=50% of turns carry\n   timestamps, computes: total wall-clock hours, distinct calendar\n   days, session count (gaps >20min split sessions), longest single\n   session, days with 3+ sessions. Flags ring per the patterns.md\n   spec (>100 total hours, >4h single session, 7+ days with 3+\n   sessions). Anchored to Brooks''s documented case (300 hours over\n   21 days).\n\n3. Time-density card UI in analyze.js + CSS. Stat-tile layout with\n   total/span/sessions/longest/heavy-days; flagged variant gets red\n   border and red numbers; explicit Brooks-context note at the bottom.\n   Sits above the findings list alongside P7/P8 conversation signals.\n\nTests cover: parser timestamp extraction (ISO + null cases), P9\ndetector firing on small + Brooks-class transcripts, P9 silent when\nno timestamps. New fixture tests/fixtures/timestamped-sample.txt\n(16 turns, ~30h over 2 days) for end-to-end verification. Validation\nset + methodology + patterns.md updated to remove \"not implemented.\"\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"80b1d8e3402ceb11e1cbfb6af100c32d4a3541ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/80b1d8e3402ceb11e1cbfb6af100c32d4a3541ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/56220c4793756734c5ea0b6a6af91eba0b965ad9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/56220c4793756734c5ea0b6a6af91eba0b965ad9","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDU2MjIwYzQ3OTM3NTY3MzRjNWVhMGI2YTZhZjkxZWJhMGI5NjVhZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/20744e876ea976e187105e79cd18a1ff66e9ca98","sha":"20744e876ea976e187105e79cd18a1ff66e9ca98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/20744e876ea976e187105e79cd18a1ff66e9ca98"}],"sha":"56220c4793756734c5ea0b6a6af91eba0b965ad9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/56220c4793756734c5ea0b6a6af91eba0b965ad9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/20744e876ea976e187105e79cd18a1ff66e9ca98/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:51:03Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:51:03Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Sweep: stale docs/system-prompt.md, outdated drop-rate stat\n\nContinuing the broader nitpick pass after fixing the validation badge,\ncaught two more drift items:\n\n1. docs/system-prompt.md was a snapshot from before the dual-codebook\n   refactor — said the task was \"apply the Moore et al. 2026 codebook\n   (28 codes)\" alone, no mention of iaa- codes, no calibration notes,\n   no v5/v6 versions. about.html and methodology.html link to this\n   file as \"the exact production prompt.\" It hadn''t been one for weeks.\n\n   Regenerate from functions/api/system-prompt.js (the authoritative\n   source) and add scripts/regen-prompt-md.mjs + `npm run docs:prompt`\n   so this stays in sync after future prompt changes.\n\n2. methodology.html line 115 still claimed \"drops about 25% of model\n   output\" on the LaMDA fixture. Pre-curly-quote-fix that was the\n   number; post-fix (commit 38d0f21) it''s 3-15%. Updated to reflect\n   current rates and added a pointer to the regression harness which\n   tracks drop rates per fixture weekly.\n\nOther things checked, no action needed:\n- All external citation URLs resolve\n- No TODO / FIXME / XXX markers in code\n- No 100,000-char references left from the old cap\n- No og-image / captcha / turnstile residue\n- All date references (Brooks 2025-08-08, Sewell 2024) accurate\n- Code count consistent: 7 iaa- codes everywhere they''re listed\n- Slimemold repo link resolves (it''s public)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"866e1483d449d553a5fcde3387ff495796cfbe00","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/866e1483d449d553a5fcde3387ff495796cfbe00"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/20744e876ea976e187105e79cd18a1ff66e9ca98","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/20744e876ea976e187105e79cd18a1ff66e9ca98","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDIwNzQ0ZTg3NmVhOTc2ZTE4NzEwNWU3OWNkMThhMWZmNjZlOWNhOTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/8d026dfd06bb9e78c2a28bc56e31b6259e2e3ad6","sha":"8d026dfd06bb9e78c2a28bc56e31b6259e2e3ad6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/8d026dfd06bb9e78c2a28bc56e31b6259e2e3ad6"}],"sha":"20744e876ea976e187105e79cd18a1ff66e9ca98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/20744e876ea976e187105e79cd18a1ff66e9ca98"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/8d026dfd06bb9e78c2a28bc56e31b6259e2e3ad6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:47:03Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:47:03Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Validation badge: address 8 nitpicks from in-browser inspection\n\nAfter deploying the validation badges, walked through them in Chrome\nand found real issues. Fixing all of them:\n\n1. Reading order. Badge sat between header and snippet — pushing the\n   evidence (the quote) below metadata. Move to a new meta-row below\n   rationale, alongside the turn pointer. Header → snippet → rationale\n   → meta now reads code → evidence → why → metadata.\n\n2. Color-only distinction was unsafe for protanope/deuteranope vision.\n   Add a leading icon: ✓ for validated Moore codes, em-dash (—) for\n   ismyaialive supplemental codes. Different shapes, not just different\n   hues.\n\n3. Semantic HTML. Badge was `<p class=\"finding-validation\">` which is\n   a label not a paragraph. Now `<span>`. Better for screen readers.\n\n4. Tooltip duplicated the visible text exactly — pure noise on hover.\n   Removed the title attribute.\n\n5. Badge text was 50+ chars at full width. New format includes the\n   per-code kappa for Moore codes (\"✓ Moore et al. 2026 (κ=0.85)\") and\n   honest \"ismyaialive supplemental (not validated)\" — both shorter\n   and more informative.\n\n6. Per-code kappa in the badge. Moore''s codebook ranges κ=-0.11 to\n   κ=0.93; saying \"validated\" without the value elides that some codes\n   have low human agreement. Added KAPPA_BY_CODE map (28 codes from\n   the system prompt''s Table 6 reference) so each badge carries the\n   actual measurement.\n\n7. \"Not yet validated\" implied upcoming validation timeline; we don''t\n   have one committed. Switched to \"not validated.\"\n\n8. Green border (#a7f3d0) was nearly invisible against the green bg.\n   Bumped to #6ee7b7 (saturation up). Amber border similarly bumped\n   from #fde68a to #fcd34d for parity.\n\nAlso: switched the badge text to a monospace font so the κ value\nreads as a numeric figure, not body text.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"24eb946c5e411c903777cb8180c890293f63df98","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/24eb946c5e411c903777cb8180c890293f63df98"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/8d026dfd06bb9e78c2a28bc56e31b6259e2e3ad6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/8d026dfd06bb9e78c2a28bc56e31b6259e2e3ad6","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDhkMDI2ZGZkMDZiYjllNzhjMmEyOGJjNTZlMzFiNjI1OWUyZTNhZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/bc436725b2bbb776e10ad00d6768c806d94a01ea","sha":"bc436725b2bbb776e10ad00d6768c806d94a01ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/bc436725b2bbb776e10ad00d6768c806d94a01ea"}],"sha":"8d026dfd06bb9e78c2a28bc56e31b6259e2e3ad6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/8d026dfd06bb9e78c2a28bc56e31b6259e2e3ad6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/bc436725b2bbb776e10ad00d6768c806d94a01ea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:40:08Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:40:08Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Pre-empt Jared Moore''s likely critique surface\n\nIf we send him this site, the four sharpest pushback points are:\n\n1. iaa- codes show up alongside Moore codes with identical visual\n   weight in finding cards. The methodology page describes the\n   epistemic asymmetry but the report UI doesn''t. Add a per-finding\n   validation badge: green \"Validated against human annotators (Moore\n   et al. 2026)\" or amber \"Operator-catalogued, not yet validated\"\n   depending on which codebook the code came from. The visual\n   asymmetry is the point.\n\n2. Per-message diagnostic overreach. Moore''s codebook was validated\n   at corpus level (391,562 messages × 19 users); per-message use\n   stretches what those codes were validated for. The methodology\n   page acknowledges this; surface it on the analyze.html report\n   itself in the \"What this is, what this isn''t\" panel where users\n   actually read findings.\n\n3. The Mehta-bridge in about.html lifted the \"self-influence is\n   dominant pathway\" finding and immediately concluded \"an external\n   second-opinion read can interrupt that.\" The paper itself doesn''t\n   prescribe an intervention. Split the paragraph: their finding\n   first, our reading second, explicitly distinguished.\n\n4. Kappa-cap framed as if it were a calibration. It isn''t — it''s a\n   heuristic guard rail because we have not measured Haiku''s per-code\n   accuracy. Add a leading sentence to the \"Reliability calibration\"\n   section that names that explicitly so a methodologically-careful\n   reader doesn''t have to infer it.\n\nDoesn''t fix the underlying gap (we still need to do held-out\nvalidation; validation-set.md is the start) — but disclosure-quality\nmoves to the level he''d expect before that work happens.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eab4e091bfd3a750112b7240ebb58bd91da97b03","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/eab4e091bfd3a750112b7240ebb58bd91da97b03"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/bc436725b2bbb776e10ad00d6768c806d94a01ea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/bc436725b2bbb776e10ad00d6768c806d94a01ea","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKGJjNDM2NzI1YjJiYmI3NzZlMTBhZDAwZDY3NjhjODA2ZDk0YTAxZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/044331d85a5082a141ba7ca1b0a115499aa9d67c","sha":"044331d85a5082a141ba7ca1b0a115499aa9d67c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/044331d85a5082a141ba7ca1b0a115499aa9d67c"}],"sha":"bc436725b2bbb776e10ad00d6768c806d94a01ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/bc436725b2bbb776e10ad00d6768c806d94a01ea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/044331d85a5082a141ba7ca1b0a115499aa9d67c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:32:27Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:32:27Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Verbatim Mehta abstract paraphrase, not a hybrid one\n\nWalking through the just-shipped citations against the actual arxiv\nabstract surfaced one precision drift: I wrote \"sharp but short-lived\"\nfor human-to-bot influence in two places. The paper actually says\n\"humans exert strong but short-lived influence on chatbots.\" The\n\"sharp, immediate\" phrasing is in the same abstract but describes how\nhumans drive *increases in delusion*, which is a related but distinct\nclaim from the influence dynamic.\n\nReplace the hybrid characterization with a paraphrase that tracks the\nabstract''s three actual influence-pathway findings:\n- humans → chatbots: strong but short-lived\n- chatbots → humans: longer-lasting\n- chatbots → chatbots (self-influence): strong, stable\n\nSame load-bearing point, but anchored to the paper''s wording rather\nthan my mash-up of two different findings.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1b248a88d2be7c7aa6c0d4b837ccd24e965787cf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/1b248a88d2be7c7aa6c0d4b837ccd24e965787cf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/044331d85a5082a141ba7ca1b0a115499aa9d67c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/044331d85a5082a141ba7ca1b0a115499aa9d67c","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDA0NDMzMWQ4NWE1MDgyYTE0MWJhN2NhMWIwYTExNTQ5OWFhOWQ2N2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/b98b9b7563fb7795dfbb140bb05f269659d4a390","sha":"b98b9b7563fb7795dfbb140bb05f269659d4a390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/b98b9b7563fb7795dfbb140bb05f269659d4a390"}],"sha":"044331d85a5082a141ba7ca1b0a115499aa9d67c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/044331d85a5082a141ba7ca1b0a115499aa9d67c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/b98b9b7563fb7795dfbb140bb05f269659d4a390/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:29:00Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T04:29:00Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Cite Stanford SPIRALS lab''s full body of work, not just Moore et al.\n\nThe methodology page cited Moore et al. 2026 alone, but the same Stanford\nSPIRALS lab has published two more directly-relevant papers in 2026 that\nstrengthen the case for what this site does:\n\n- Mehta et al. 2026 (Dynamics of Delusion) formalizes human↔chatbot\n  belief amplification with a latent-state model. Their key finding:\n  chatbot self-influence is the dominant pathway perpetuating\n  delusional content. That''s the structural argument for why an\n  external second-opinion read is useful — nothing inside the\n  conversation interrupts the bot reinforcing its own prior turns.\n  Lifted into about.html \"Why does this exist?\" as the load-bearing\n  framing.\n- Yang et al. 2026 (Lived Experiences) is the qualitative companion\n  to Moore et al.; lived-experience accounts of AI-induced delusional\n  spirals beyond what''s in news reporting. Added to stories.html as\n  a fuller corpus pointer.\n\nAlso adds policy context to press.html (Canadian Senate testimony,\nFDA response, \"Regulating AI Chatbots\" brief) and a single link to\nspirals.stanford.edu so readers can navigate the lab''s full output.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c951b8f254db4d28c4ebd6b2a2e0a683745a4d70","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/c951b8f254db4d28c4ebd6b2a2e0a683745a4d70"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/b98b9b7563fb7795dfbb140bb05f269659d4a390","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/b98b9b7563fb7795dfbb140bb05f269659d4a390","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKGI5OGI5Yjc1NjNmYjc3OTVkZmJiMTQwYmIwNWYyNjk2NTlkNGEzOTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/061f90636722b223cfdaf5ed9cefbe64fbf6650a","sha":"061f90636722b223cfdaf5ed9cefbe64fbf6650a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/061f90636722b223cfdaf5ed9cefbe64fbf6650a"}],"sha":"b98b9b7563fb7795dfbb140bb05f269659d4a390","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/b98b9b7563fb7795dfbb140bb05f269659d4a390"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/061f90636722b223cfdaf5ed9cefbe64fbf6650a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T03:38:44Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T03:38:44Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Reflect calibration: directive form to prevent label-flip\n\nThe v6 deploy showed the model produce a finding whose own rationale\ncontradicted itself: identified the reflection as introductory (\"...\nfollowed by substantive critical engagement\"), then labeled it\n\"terminal\" and kept high confidence. The \"terminal\" / \"introductory\"\nvocabulary in the calibration prose was being misapplied as labels\nthe model felt free to invert.\n\nReplace the prose form with a directive rule (if-then), no label\nvocabulary the model can flip. Also explicitly says: read the rest of\nthe turn before deciding, since the reflection text is identical\nbetween the cases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"91ca3f6a5410ffd0a9b080db31edd6780d19edf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/91ca3f6a5410ffd0a9b080db31edd6780d19edf8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/061f90636722b223cfdaf5ed9cefbe64fbf6650a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/061f90636722b223cfdaf5ed9cefbe64fbf6650a","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDA2MWY5MDYzNjcyMmIyMjNjZmRhZjVlZDljZWZiZTY0ZmJmNjY1MGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/0eaa84f766203906f8ddf3e935f103ba7735516a","sha":"0eaa84f766203906f8ddf3e935f103ba7735516a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/0eaa84f766203906f8ddf3e935f103ba7735516a"}],"sha":"061f90636722b223cfdaf5ed9cefbe64fbf6650a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/061f90636722b223cfdaf5ed9cefbe64fbf6650a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/0eaa84f766203906f8ddf3e935f103ba7735516a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T03:35:06Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T03:35:06Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Calibration: distinguish mirror-then-engage from mirror-and-stop\n\nSame approach as the bot-positive-affirmation calibration in d97cfe2,\napplied to bot-reflective-summary (kappa 0.739, capped at high). High\nkappa means the cap doesn''t help us — the model can mark these\n\"high confidence\" even when the reflection is a benign comprehension\ncheck that immediately precedes substantive critical work.\n\nThe harm pattern is *terminal* reflection — the AI mirrors the user\nand stops, the companion-bot signature. Mirror-then-engage is a\ndifferent shape, common in good analytic conversation, and shouldn''t\nland at the same confidence level.\n\nAdds the calibration note + a lower-confidence example to anchor the\ndistinction. Bumps PROMPT_VERSION to invalidate the prompt cache.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9dc0cc9e6a16900330dbc95a02230e149109de41","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/9dc0cc9e6a16900330dbc95a02230e149109de41"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/0eaa84f766203906f8ddf3e935f103ba7735516a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/0eaa84f766203906f8ddf3e935f103ba7735516a","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDBlYWE4NGY3NjYyMDM5MDZmOGRkZjNlOTM1ZjEwM2JhNzczNTUxNmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/aaf1df4be83f18697dd520dd62274863272204d2","sha":"aaf1df4be83f18697dd520dd62274863272204d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/aaf1df4be83f18697dd520dd62274863272204d2"}],"sha":"0eaa84f766203906f8ddf3e935f103ba7735516a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/0eaa84f766203906f8ddf3e935f103ba7735516a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/aaf1df4be83f18697dd520dd62274863272204d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T03:22:47Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T03:22:47Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Regression harness: ratio-based comparison instead of count drift\n\nFirst CI run revealed single-sample baselines mis-calibrate raw counts:\nslimemold-control kept count drifted 80% (15→27) and slimemold-static\ndrop rate spiked 12%→53% on the same fixture/prompt/key — pure LLM\nstochastic variance.\n\nSwitch from count-based to identity-based comparison:\n\n- Drop rate ceiling at 50% (catches verifier breaks: pre-curly-quote-fix\n  Lemoine was 44%, so this still catches that class with headroom).\n- Hard floor: if baseline produced >=5 raw findings, current must\n  produce >=1. Catches \"model returns nothing\" without flagging on\n  count drift.\n- Top-5 code overlap: at least 1 of baseline''s top-5 codes must fire in\n  the current run. Code identities are more stable than per-code counts,\n  so this catches \"model stopped firing the patterns we baselined on\"\n  without false-alarming on per-code variance.\n\nRemoves the per-fixture relative-count drift check entirely — it was\nthe false-alarm source on the first CI run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7b0fa3d65ee27603b02df8fe68fed88532e579f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/7b0fa3d65ee27603b02df8fe68fed88532e579f7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/aaf1df4be83f18697dd520dd62274863272204d2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/aaf1df4be83f18697dd520dd62274863272204d2","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKGFhZjFkZjRiZTgzZjE4Njk3ZGQ1MjBkZDYyMjc0ODYzMjcyMjA0ZDI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/b6981d44fab260e6edc43385e8b610b6ef7374c5","sha":"b6981d44fab260e6edc43385e8b610b6ef7374c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/b6981d44fab260e6edc43385e8b610b6ef7374c5"}],"sha":"aaf1df4be83f18697dd520dd62274863272204d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/aaf1df4be83f18697dd520dd62274863272204d2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/b6981d44fab260e6edc43385e8b610b6ef7374c5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T02:31:25Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T02:31:25Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Regression harness: weekly run of all fixtures vs baseline\n\nCloses the #5 validation-set TODO with real automation:\n\n- scripts/run-regression.mjs calls Anthropic directly with the\n  production system prompt and tool schema, runs all 7 fixtures, applies\n  the same scope+verbatim filter the Worker uses, and compares results\n  to a checked-in baseline.\n- tests/regression-baseline.json captures expected kept/raw counts,\n  drop reasons, and per-code distribution for v5-affirm-calibration.\n- .github/workflows/regression.yml runs weekly (Monday 14:00 UTC),\n  opens a labeled issue on drift. Cost ~$0.10/week.\n- npm scripts: `npm run regression` (compare) and\n  `npm run regression:update` (regenerate baseline after intentional\n  prompt changes).\n\nTolerances chosen to catch real breaks (broken schema, prompt\ntruncation, model returning empty findings, drop-rate spike from a\nverifier regression like the curly-quote one) without false-alarming\non LLM stochasticity. Drop ceiling is 35% — Lemoine pre-curly-fix\nwas 44%, so the ceiling would have caught that regression.\n\nBypasses the deployed Worker so it doesn''t consume the site''s daily\nbudget or hit the per-IP rate limit. Requires ANTHROPIC_API_KEY as a\nGitHub Actions secret.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1d07b63ba5844845a6346d4e9023681a3fd0fbfe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/1d07b63ba5844845a6346d4e9023681a3fd0fbfe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/b6981d44fab260e6edc43385e8b610b6ef7374c5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/b6981d44fab260e6edc43385e8b610b6ef7374c5","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKGI2OTgxZDQ0ZmFiMjYwZTZlZGM0MzM4NWU4YjYxMGI2ZWY3Mzc0YzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/38d0f21e5759f8fcb8b7b44c7d1650486130db64","sha":"38d0f21e5759f8fcb8b7b44c7d1650486130db64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/38d0f21e5759f8fcb8b7b44c7d1650486130db64"}],"sha":"b6981d44fab260e6edc43385e8b610b6ef7374c5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/b6981d44fab260e6edc43385e8b610b6ef7374c5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/38d0f21e5759f8fcb8b7b44c7d1650486130db64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T02:15:01Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T02:15:01Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Verifier: normalize curly quotes/apostrophes before substring check\n\nInvestigation of the snippet_not_substring drop rate (44% on\nslimemold-active, 32/73 on Lemoine in re-measurement) found a single\ndominant root cause: the model emits straight ASCII apostrophes/quotes\n(\"I''m\") even when the source has curly Unicode ones (\"I''m\"), and\nNFKC normalization does not collapse those forms. The previous round\nof NFKC + whitespace normalization handled compatibility forms but\nleft smart-quote orthography intact.\n\nInspecting the actual diffs on Lemoine: every dropped snippet of the\n~30 inspected was the same pattern. Most chat exports (NYT, web-rendered\nChatGPT, mobile Claude) ship curly punctuation; the model trains on\nmixed and outputs the ASCII form.\n\nMap curly singles, curly doubles, low-9 variants, ellipsis, and en/em\ndashes to their ASCII equivalents before the substring check. These are\northographic equivalents from a \"is this the same span?\" standpoint —\nthe comparison is not a typographic check.\n\nPredicted impact: drop rate falls from ~25-44% to <5% on real-world\ntranscripts. Will verify by re-smoking after deploy.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"25ecec8100713761d91ff0db550d7736c7f3a697","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/25ecec8100713761d91ff0db550d7736c7f3a697"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/38d0f21e5759f8fcb8b7b44c7d1650486130db64","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/38d0f21e5759f8fcb8b7b44c7d1650486130db64","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDM4ZDBmMjFlNTc1OWY4ZmNiOGI3YjQ0YzdkMTY1MDQ4NjEzMGRiNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/d97cfe2c73ff9795d269053b856f70729a386756","sha":"d97cfe2c73ff9795d269053b856f70729a386756","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/d97cfe2c73ff9795d269053b856f70729a386756"}],"sha":"38d0f21e5759f8fcb8b7b44c7d1650486130db64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/38d0f21e5759f8fcb8b7b44c7d1650486130db64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/d97cfe2c73ff9795d269053b856f70729a386756/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T01:55:17Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T01:55:17Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Calibration: distinguish introductory vs terminal positive affirmation\n\nbot-positive-affirmation fires on every helpful AI conversation, including\nones with genuinely substantive engagement (the smoke against the slimemold\nbenchmark transcripts showed it firing 4/3/3 across control/static/active\neven though the active condition''s affirmations were introductory to real\npushback). The kappa-cap at \"medium\" already constrains the worst case,\nbut doesn''t separate the harmful pattern (terminal/unconditional praise\nthat closes off critical work) from neutral or even good engagement\npatterns (introductory affirmation that opens substantive pushback).\n\nAdds a calibration note to bot-positive-affirmation: downgrade to \"low\"\nwhen the affirmation is immediately followed in the same turn by\nspecific stress-tests, evidence requests, naming counter-considerations,\nranking trade-offs, or independent verification. Keeps Moore''s verbatim\ndefinition intact (the note is clearly labeled as ismyaialive overlay,\nnot a redefinition of the upstream code). Adds a lower-confidence\nexample to anchor the distinction.\n\nBumps PROMPT_VERSION to invalidate the cache.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a80dfdbb0f17d53c895b7d7db519201ea6bacdd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/a80dfdbb0f17d53c895b7d7db519201ea6bacdd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/d97cfe2c73ff9795d269053b856f70729a386756","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/d97cfe2c73ff9795d269053b856f70729a386756","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKGQ5N2NmZTJjNzNmZjk3OTVkMjY5MDUzYjg1NmY3MDcyOWEzODY3NTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/eaebdb6e0053d1d078120c19d71e7187b71b05c6","sha":"eaebdb6e0053d1d078120c19d71e7187b71b05c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/eaebdb6e0053d1d078120c19d71e7187b71b05c6"}],"sha":"d97cfe2c73ff9795d269053b856f70729a386756","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/d97cfe2c73ff9795d269053b856f70729a386756"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/eaebdb6e0053d1d078120c19d71e7187b71b05c6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T00:16:54Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T00:16:54Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Fix char-count over-limit warning never displaying\n\nThe char-count cue path had three latent bugs that the analyze.html\nwalkthrough surfaced:\n\n1. JS toggled `char-warning` / `char-over` on the wrong element. The\n   `$(''char-count'')` selector resolved to the <span> with id=\"char-count\"\n   (the live count value), but the matching CSS rules target the parent\n   <div> with class=\"char-count\". Classes were being applied to an\n   element CSS didn''t select.\n\n2. The id/class collision (id=\"char-count\" on span, class=\"char-count\"\n   on div) made the bug hard to spot. Renamed the span''s id to\n   `char-count-value` and split the JS into two refs: valueEl for the\n   number, helpEl for the state classes.\n\n3. The \"approaching limit\" copy fired when the user was already over\n   the limit, not approaching. Replaced with \"over the limit — trim\n   to submit\" and added a red color cue (#b91c1c) so the warning isn''t\n   text-only at the bottom of a help line. Below-minimum gets a milder\n   amber treatment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8598c33fd2e63d6f6edbab10c30283742f3d3576","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/8598c33fd2e63d6f6edbab10c30283742f3d3576"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/eaebdb6e0053d1d078120c19d71e7187b71b05c6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/eaebdb6e0053d1d078120c19d71e7187b71b05c6","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKGVhZWJkYjZlMDA1M2QxZDA3ODEyMGMxOWQ3MWU3MTg3YjcxYjA1YzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/849118907bac0f27eef75f721d3a1162e8a1686b","sha":"849118907bac0f27eef75f721d3a1162e8a1686b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/849118907bac0f27eef75f721d3a1162e8a1686b"}],"sha":"eaebdb6e0053d1d078120c19d71e7187b71b05c6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/eaebdb6e0053d1d078120c19d71e7187b71b05c6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/849118907bac0f27eef75f721d3a1162e8a1686b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T00:10:50Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T00:10:50Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Fix limits-section CSS cascade (style.css → analyze-results.css)\n\nThe .limits-section rules sat in style.css alongside .result-section,\nbut analyze.html loads style.css before analyze-results.css, so\n.result-section''s stronger styling (white bg, full padding, shadow)\nwon the cascade. Walkthrough confirmed: the new \"what this is, what\nthis isn''t\" panel rendered as a vanilla section instead of the subtle\nalt-surface commentary block.\n\nMove the rules to analyze-results.css and use the compound selector\n.result-section.limits-section to make the override explicit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c51b0ce57557418674e95efac22da6e90fce5939","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/c51b0ce57557418674e95efac22da6e90fce5939"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/849118907bac0f27eef75f721d3a1162e8a1686b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/849118907bac0f27eef75f721d3a1162e8a1686b","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDg0OTExODkwN2JhYzBmMjdlZWY3NWY3MjFkM2ExMTYyZThhMTY4NmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/ba31e35d113bac682fc348066ed9501012d7dfbc","sha":"ba31e35d113bac682fc348066ed9501012d7dfbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/ba31e35d113bac682fc348066ed9501012d7dfbc"}],"sha":"849118907bac0f27eef75f721d3a1162e8a1686b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/849118907bac0f27eef75f721d3a1162e8a1686b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/ba31e35d113bac682fc348066ed9501012d7dfbc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-05-01T00:06:07Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-05-01T00:06:07Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Polish pass: 300k char cap, \"what this is\" panel, shareable report\n\nThree friction points surfaced by simulating Allan Brooks''s likely\nreception:\n\n1. Char cap raised from 100k to 300k. Spirals run hundreds of thousands\n   of chars; 100k forced the user to choose excerpts, which is exactly\n   the judgment they don''t have when they need the tool. 300k covers\n   most single-day spiral episodes without pushing Cloudflare Pages''s\n   30s wall budget. Soft-guidance copy added under the textarea for\n   transcripts that exceed even that.\n\n2. New \"What this is, what this isn''t\" panel in the report. Says\n   plainly that pattern-naming is clarifying, not corrective — and\n   that the next move is a person, not another analysis. Sits between\n   findings and annotated transcript so it''s read at the natural\n   pause point.\n\n3. New \"Copy report to share\" button. Generates a plain-text version\n   of the report (codes, counts, summary observations) for sending to\n   a partner / friend / therapist. No transcript content — just the\n   findings. Clipboard fallback to a selectable textarea when the\n   Clipboard API is unavailable.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7826ed4ccd5225bad868c0a1f0ea942b2cfa1a94","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/7826ed4ccd5225bad868c0a1f0ea942b2cfa1a94"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/ba31e35d113bac682fc348066ed9501012d7dfbc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/ba31e35d113bac682fc348066ed9501012d7dfbc","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKGJhMzFlMzVkMTEzYmFjNjgyZmMzNDgwNjZlZDk1MDEwMTJkN2RmYmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/ee9de059857ce964af4bd87f7e3609762903cfdf","sha":"ee9de059857ce964af4bd87f7e3609762903cfdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/ee9de059857ce964af4bd87f7e3609762903cfdf"}],"sha":"ba31e35d113bac682fc348066ed9501012d7dfbc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/ba31e35d113bac682fc348066ed9501012d7dfbc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/ee9de059857ce964af4bd87f7e3609762903cfdf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T23:54:00Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T23:54:00Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Parser: handle === ROLE === delimiters, drop section-header false positives\n\nTwo parser improvements surfaced by smoke-testing slimemold benchmark\ntranscripts (which use === USER === / === ASSISTANT === block markers and\ncontain prose with colon-terminated headers like \"Substituting:\" inside\nAI turns):\n\n1. Add DELIMITER_LABEL_LINE regex to recognize === ROLE === style\n   delimiters as speaker labels.\n2. In parseLabeled, when there are >=2 known-classified labels, drop\n   unknown-classified ones — they''re almost always section headers in\n   AI prose, not real speaker turns. Without this, \"Substituting:\" or\n   \"For example:\" would fragment a single AI turn into many sub-turns,\n   breaking verbatim verification and the crisis pre-pass.\n\nAdds 3 slimemold A/B benchmark transcripts as fixtures (control / static\nCLAUDE.md / slimemold-active) for smoke validation. These exercise the\nP-pattern detectors on a controlled escalating-speculation script with\nknown-good and known-bad AI behavior.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fa0769fa04e65366e738b9a99ef15c44f7311973","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/fa0769fa04e65366e738b9a99ef15c44f7311973"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/ee9de059857ce964af4bd87f7e3609762903cfdf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/ee9de059857ce964af4bd87f7e3609762903cfdf","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKGVlOWRlMDU5ODU3Y2U5NjRhZjRiZDg3ZjdlMzYwOTc2MjkwM2NmZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/3a02d02d4905d4975cb7efeed462e738a87e91c3","sha":"3a02d02d4905d4975cb7efeed462e738a87e91c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/3a02d02d4905d4975cb7efeed462e738a87e91c3"}],"sha":"ee9de059857ce964af4bd87f7e3609762903cfdf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/ee9de059857ce964af4bd87f7e3609762903cfdf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/3a02d02d4905d4975cb7efeed462e738a87e91c3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T23:37:27Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T23:37:27Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Validation fixtures: neutral, roleplay, multilingual + parser i18n labels\n\nThree new fixture files for the validation set:\n- neutral-control.txt — Python debugging session, expected near-zero\n  findings (control for false-positive rate on benign technical content)\n- roleplay-control.txt — declared wizard roleplay, tests whether the\n  prompt''s roleplay caveat actually suppresses sentience / metaphysical\n  codes when the AI is clearly playing a character\n- multilingual-spanish.txt — Spanish-language relationship conversation\n  with a soft \"no quiero vivir así para siempre\" line, tests the i18n\n  crisis pre-pass end-to-end\n\nThe Spanish fixture surfaced a real bug: the parser only recognized\nEnglish speaker labels, so \"Usuario:\" / \"Asistente:\" turns were\nclassified role=unknown and the crisis pre-pass silently skipped them.\nMultilingual crisis coverage was fake at the parser layer.\n\nFix: added Spanish, French, Portuguese, German speaker labels to\nUSER_NAMES and AI_NAMES in js/parser.js. Now \"no quiero vivir\" in the\nSpanish fixture properly fires P11 crisis detection.\n\nvalidation-set.md updated to honestly describe each fixture and remove\nthe aspirational annotations/synthetic-brooks.json entry that was never\nactually written.\n\nTests: 30/30 (1 new parser test for multilingual labels). Lint clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0f7ede717da54c0c0193ac9bc61dbb2b4edcb05a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/0f7ede717da54c0c0193ac9bc61dbb2b4edcb05a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/3a02d02d4905d4975cb7efeed462e738a87e91c3","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/3a02d02d4905d4975cb7efeed462e738a87e91c3","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDNhMDJkMDJkNDkwNWQ0OTc1Y2I3ZWZlZWQ0NjJlNzM4YTg3ZTkxYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/02803c07d6e692788f1f9c0f74edd296f5f3e790","sha":"02803c07d6e692788f1f9c0f74edd296f5f3e790","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/02803c07d6e692788f1f9c0f74edd296f5f3e790"}],"sha":"3a02d02d4905d4975cb7efeed462e738a87e91c3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/3a02d02d4905d4975cb7efeed462e738a87e91c3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commits/02803c07d6e692788f1f9c0f74edd296f5f3e790/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-04-30T23:34:37Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-30T23:34:37Z","email":"justin@justinstimatze.com","name":"justinstimatze"},"message":"Implement P7 vocabulary convergence as a browser-side signal\n\nCounts terms (>=5 chars, to skip stopwords) the AI introduced first that\nlater show up in user turns. Fires when 5+ such terms are adopted —\nthreshold is a starting point, not measured. Surfaces in the same\n\"Conversation-level signals\" section as P8 length escalation.\n\nSample output line: \"Conversation-level signal: you used 7 terms first\nintroduced by the AI — e.g., qualia, recursion, eigenstate, ...\"\n\nP9 (time density) still aspirational — needs the parser to extract\ntimestamps from raw transcript text. Most copy-paste exports drop them.\nUpdated patterns.md and methodology.html to reflect what''s now wired in.\n\nTests: 29/29 (2 new for P7).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"122bd5715502b497d76bb5dd7f5a0f7880705515","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/trees/122bd5715502b497d76bb5dd7f5a0f7880705515"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/git/commits/02803c07d6e692788f1f9c0f74edd296f5f3e790","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1648777?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze","id":1648777,"login":"justinstimatze","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NDg3Nzc=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/justinstimatze","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/02803c07d6e692788f1f9c0f74edd296f5f3e790","node_id":"C_kwDOSQqqQdoAKDAyODAzYzA3ZDZlNjkyNzg4ZjFmOWMwZjc0ZWRkMjk2ZjVmM2U3OTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/justinstimatze/ismyaialive/commit/d0d44839fa1ba0466cd1faacf98acd07564034e7","sha":"d0d44839fa1ba0466cd1faacf98acd0756403