commit/774f3f0bb0896d54f85fdf5a65d8f5daa1d75f1d","node_id":"C_kwDOSQth5toAKDc3NGYzZjBiYjA4OTZkNTRmODVmZGY1YTY1ZDhmNWRhYTFkNzVmMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/commit/6d4cc1b93141372d001fefb966891a61e8da2687","sha":"6d4cc1b93141372d001fefb966891a61e8da2687","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/commits/6d4cc1b93141372d001fefb966891a61e8da2687"}],"sha":"774f3f0bb0896d54f85fdf5a65d8f5daa1d75f1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/commits/774f3f0bb0896d54f85fdf5a65d8f5daa1d75f1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/stellarshenson","id":18424023,"login":"stellarshenson","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4NDI0MDIz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/commits/6d4cc1b93141372d001fefb966891a61e8da2687/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-16T11:11:00Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-16T11:11:00Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"fix: tint a terminal from its own conversation, not the project row (DEF-11)\n\nA session''s terminal tab was tinted, then lost its colour after some time -\na regression introduced in 1.2.45.\n\nReading the true session id from the pidfile made a bare `claude -c` report\nits real conversation, which moved it out of the cwd fallback (that had been\ntinting it by accident) and into the exact-id branch. That branch matched the\nterminal''s conversation against the panel rows, but a row carries only the\nproject''s representative conversation, and the representative flips to any\nnewer JSONL - a daemon --fork-session worker writes one - so the terminal\nmatched no row and the exact-id miss cleared the tint.\n\n- terminal-cwd now returns the colour of the conversation the terminal RUNS,\n  read from that conversation''s own JSONL (_session_colour, glob-escaped so\n  the id is a file name and never a pattern); the frontend uses it directly,\n  retiring the row lookup and with it the fork, sibling-borrow and\n  nested-project failure classes\n- _interrogateTerminal no longer short-circuits on the launch cache, which\n  pinned a panel-launched tab to its launch-time conversation\n- colour selection extracted to src/colour.ts, kept JupyterLab-free so jest\n  can execute it: the tint path had zero coverage, which is how DEF-10 and\n  DEF-11 both shipped green. Now 100% line-covered\n- survived a two-round qa-engineer adversarial review. Round 1 blocked on the\n  color wire key being pinned at no tier (deleting it reproduced DEF-11 with\n  pytest green) and on the new jest tests being exact-text pins that went red\n  on a correct refactor; both fixed, round 2 clean\n\npytest 111, jest 64, tsc + lint clean.","tree":{"sha":"bbbcc4ab21122b670510fcfdd707ca7831b4e691","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/git/trees/bbbcc4ab21122b670510fcfdd707ca7831b4e691"},"url":"https://api.github.com/rep