received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/commits/3ccbb7ef233008655c66afea262e5d41d6f10762/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-15T21:38:54Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-15T21:38:54Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"fix: reuse a Claude terminal by its true session id (DEF-9 case c)\n\nClicking a project row that already had a user-opened `claude -c` or bare\nterminal spawned a duplicate instead of focusing the running one. The reuse\ngate read the conversation id only from process argv (--session-id /\n--resume), which the panel injects but a self-opened terminal never carries,\nso the running terminal reported a null id, failed the strict match, and a\nfresh duplicate launched (the colour path''s cwd fallback still tinted it,\nmasking the miss).\n\n- backend reads the true sessionId from ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json,\n  written for every interactive session regardless of launch flags, with\n  argv only a fallback (_session_id_from_pidfile, _claude_session_id)\n- frontend _findTerminalForSession matches on the session id alone, dropping\n  the cwd sanity-gate as itself an overfit\n- pytest 107, jest 58, tsc + lint clean","tree":{"sha":"eec6c6b8fc5eb00468b9b05679894deda35b856b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/git/trees/eec6c6b8fc5eb00468b9b05679894deda35b856b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/git/commits/3ccbb7ef233008655c66afea262e5d41d6f10762