//api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/commits/441d8d9784db2ecce1f50308e880ee93414fbed7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-13T13:14:04Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-13T13:14:04Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"feat: tint each Claude terminal tab with its session colour\n\n- read the Claude session colour (set via /color, else auto-assigned) from the\n  session JSONL and surface it as a per-row `color` field\n  (`_scan_jsonl_for_agent_color` tail-scan in `sessions.py`)\n- delegate the tab tint to `jupyterlab_colourful_tab_extension` via its new\n  `IColourfulTabs.setColour` token API (singleton shared dependency ^1.0.19)\n  rather than owning tab CSS, so the two extensions never fight over tab classes\n- map claude colour names to colourful-tab ids (red->rose, orange->peach,\n  yellow->lemon, green->mint, blue->sky, purple->lavender) and retint open\n  Claude terminals on fetch and the 30s poll (`_reconcileTerminalColours`)\n- record DEF-9 (opening an already-open session can spawn a duplicate resume)\n  in docs/defects.md with root cause and deferred fix options","tree":{"sha":"af53273af149cfc07c80091230d45d6f2396e40a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/git/trees/af53273af149cfc07c80091230d45d6f2396e40a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/git/commits/441d8d9784db2ecce1f50308e880ee93414fbed7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","follow