pi.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/commits/8d3ccf73fdaa4c3f64972587a5a12b1130edb28f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-03T08:50:44Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-03T08:50:44Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"fix: gate the remote-control indicator on session freshness (DEF-8)\n\nThe green \"remote control active\" dot stayed lit for a bridged session that\nhad gone idle - e.g. a project last active 17 days ago still showed it.\n\nClaude leaves bridgeSessionId set in ~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json after the\nbridge disconnects while the interactive process keeps running, so the DEF-7\ngate (live pid AND non-null bridgeSessionId) still passed a stale zombie. There\nis no idle heartbeat - the pid file is rewritten only on a busy/idle status\ntransition, which fires on every turn whether local or remote - so updatedAt\nfreshness is the only signal the bridge is being driven now.\n\n- session_state_by_cwd now also requires the record to be active within\n  REMOTE_CONTROL_FRESH_MS (1 hour)\n- test updated with a stale-but-bridged case; DEF-8 registered in docs/defects.md","tree":{"sha":"183dcf79452c23c7953a968fbaec03fc06fd90b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/git/trees/183dcf79452c23c7953a968fbaec03fc06fd90b8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/git/commits/8d3ccf73fdaa4c3f64972587a5a12b1130edb28f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}"