s/f102dbd403b038899150d229bc6280bd72dd51af/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-07-01T13:20:41Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-07-01T13:20:41Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"fix: only light the remote-control indicator for bridged sessions (DEF-7)\n\nThe panel''s green \"remote control active\" dot lit for any session with a\nlive claude process registered for its cwd. But claude 2.x writes a\n~/.claude/sessions/<pid>.json for every interactive session; the\nremote-control (\"bridge\") link is signalled by a non-null bridgeSessionId.\nA plain interactive claude therefore falsely showed the indicator.\n\n- sessions.py: session_state_by_cwd reads bridgeSessionId and sets\n  remote_control only when the record is both live and bridged; list_sessions\n  consumes the flag instead of raw pid liveness\n- test_routes.py: assert the bridged rule (live+bridged True, live-unbridged\n  and dead-bridged both False)\n- README: describe the dot as remote-control, not merely running\n- docs: consolidate defects into the lean master docs/defects.md, register\n  DEF-7 (fixed), update acc-crit links","tree":{"sha":"0d8f3b3db7e14425b10f59f39923b86cc5025106","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/git/trees/0d8f3b3db7e14425b10f59f39923b86cc5025106"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/git/commits/f102dbd403b038899150d229bc6280bd72dd51af","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18424023?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.