.github.com/users/stellarshenson/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/stellarshenson","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/stellarshenson/jupyterlab_claude_code_extension/commits/fa257a2c12f73cc3179002609fc11784e1044ef3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-22T07:44:33Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-22T07:44:33Z","email":"konrad.jelen@gmail.com","name":"stellarshenson"},"message":"feat: conversation-aware terminal reuse and Open Branched Conversation\n\n- fix (DEF-3): clicking a row after switching to another conversation\n  resumed the original one - terminal reuse was keyed purely by project\n  cwd, so the still-open claude --resume <original> terminal was refocused\n  regardless of the switched branch (a running claude is pinned to one\n  conversation). The terminal-cwd endpoint now reports the running claude''s\n  conversation id from its /proc argv (--session-id for a fork, else\n  --resume); reuse matches only a terminal running the wanted conversation -\n  lenient for the current row, strict for opening a specific branch\n- feat: Open Branched Conversation submenu (top 5) and a per-row Open button\n  in the Manage Sessions popup launch any conversation directly in its own\n  terminal, so several branches of one project run independently\n- a freshly forked branch now surfaces within seconds via a bounded fast\n  watcher instead of waiting for the 30s poll\n- backend _parse_resume_id/_claude_resume_id with pytest; jest contracts and\n  Galata UI specs; acc-crit Open Branched Conversation section and DEF-3\n\nSurvived /adversarial-review (2 rounds): fixed the microcache storing the wanted not observed id and a strict ''already in use'' on the current row; round 2 SHIP.","tree":{"sha":"4c0031f2504fcd2b94dd16853db2690ba8e7740b","ur