n completa LoaderAdapter type=''web-component''\n\nwebComponentLoader const MicroFrontendLoaderAdapter completo D-V2-F15-05..08:\n\nStep 1-2 (validation):\n- url string non-empty → altrimenti MF_WC_SCRIPT_LOAD_FAILED\n- elementName regex /^[a-z][a-z0-9._-]*-[a-z0-9._-]*$/ kebab-case con almeno un dash (WHATWG spec) → altrimenti MF_WC_SCRIPT_LOAD_FAILED\n- contextMode ∈ {''property'',''attribute'',''event''} default ''property'' (D-V2-F15-05) → altrimenti MF_WC_CONTEXT_MODE_INVALID\n- timeoutMs default 15000 ms + defensive (non-finiti o <=0 → fall-back default)\n\nStep 3 (reuse-on-collision D-V2-F15-08):\n- customElements.get(elementName) pre-check → se già definito: console.warn ''[mf-wc] custom element NAME already defined — reusing existing registration for mfId=ID'' + return reused klass + metadata.reused: true. NO throw (warning-level — supporta multi-mount + shared design system primitives).\n\nStep 4 (ESM import D-V2-F15-07 carryover F9):\n- combineSignals(ctx.signal, AbortSignal.timeout(timeoutMs)) composite\n- Promise.race([import(url) /* @vite-ignore */, abortPromise(composite)])\n- Discriminate timeout vs consumer abort vs network/parse/CSP error\n- Tutti i casi → MF_WC_SCRIPT_LOAD_FAILED con originalError preservato (per import rejection)\n\nStep 5 (whenDefined race D-V2-F15-06):\n- awaitDefined(elementName, ctx.signal, timeoutMs) — happy path resolve immediato (step 4 ha già fatto define); timeout → MF_WC_DEFINE_TIMEOUT\n\nStep 6 (LoadedModule):\n- module: CustomElementConstructor + lifecycle wrapper (mount/unmount) + metadata {elementName, contextMode, timeoutMs, reused, url}\n\nLifecycle wrapper interno (createLifecycleWrapper):\n- mount(ctx): document.createElement(elementName) + applyContext(el, ctx.context, mode) + WeakMap track per unmount lookup\n- unmount(ctx): WeakMap lookup → element.remove() + cleanup\n- MOUNTED_ELEMENTS WeakMap<MicroFrontendRuntimeContext, HTMLElement> — reference identity ctx mount↔unmount\n\nD-V2-F15-05 (default property), 