{getCircuitState, getRetryAttempts} → ctx.registerService(SERVICE_FALLBACKS)\n    (5) orchestratorChain async: circuit check → retry check (skip runtime/update OQ-1)\n        → fallback render dispatch + success path emit microfrontend.recovered + reset\n        counter + recordSuccess\n    (6) installErrorSubscribe(broker, {dispatch: orchestratorChain, signal: ctrl.signal})\n    (7) subscribe microfrontend.unregistered cleanup P-02: circuitBreaker.dispose +\n        retryEngine.resetCounter su tutte le 7 phases\n    (8) AbortSignal cleanup cascade D-V2-16: ctrl.signal abort → unsubscribe all +\n        shutdownSignal opt forwarding host responsibility\n  - W11 defensive guard `typeof op !== ''function''` documentato future-proof (unreachable\n    via phase filter — belt-and-suspenders contro F15+ API surface changes).\n  - Anti-singleton D-30: ogni call ritorna nuovo BrokerModule.\n  - Closure capture narrowing fix: const alias `mfService: MicroFrontendsService`\n    post-narrowing per preservare type nel orchestratorChain async closure (TS18048\n    fix).\n\n- fallbacks-module.test.ts (~420 LoC, 17 test): Tier-1 integration suite coverage:\n  - 2 test factory shape (id ''fallbacks'' + install function + anti-singleton D-30).\n  - 5 test install flow (SERVICE_MICROFRONTENDS lookup throw + idempotent guard +\n    service register + getRetryAttempts default 0 + getCircuitState default ''closed'').\n  - 2 test full chain integration (error event → dispatch → publish event topic +\n    emit microfrontend.fallback.rendered post dispatch).\n  - 2 test cleanup P-02 (microfrontend.unregistered con id + con microFrontendId\n    alternative key entrambi supportati).\n  - 1 test W8 retry success path D-V2-F14-12 (Scenario 12): retry success → emit\n    microfrontend.recovered + reset counter + recordSuccess (closed default).\n  - 2 test skip retry runtime/update OQ-1 (runtime.failed + update.failed → dispatch\n    fallback diretto no setTimeout retry).\n  - 1 test no fallback policy → emit fallbackType:''none'' (observability).\n  - 2 test descriptor.fallback override defaultPolicy (precedence + fallback to\n    defaultPolicy quando descriptor.fallback assente).\n\nCoverage REQ-IDs CLOSED:\n- MF-FALLBACK-01: MicroFrontendFallbackPolicy 6-onXError scope wire reale via\n  getDefinitionForPhase mapping + descriptor.fallback override + options.defaultPolicy\n  carryover.\n- MF-FALLBACK-05: 4 rendering modes (html target chain + isolation respect; component\n  Service Locator F15 stub fallback; event broker.publish con source D-23; custom\n  await + try/catch) + none observability emit unificato microfrontend.fallback.rendered.\n\nAcceptance Task 3:\n- pnpm --filter @gluezero/fallbacks test esit 0 (130 test PASS — 84 baseline + 29\n  fallback-renderer + 17 fallbacks-module).\n- pnpm --filter @gluezero/fallbacks typecheck esit 0.\n- pnpm --filter @gluezero/fallbacks build esit 0 (dist/index.js 9.47 KB un-gzipped).\n- D-83 strict septuple zero-diff verificato (git diff 8f6b4b7..HEAD -- 7-protected = 0\n  lines).\n\nPlan-test deviation Rule 1: planner test code aveva `expect(mod.name)...` ma il\nBrokerModule contract @gluezero/core usa `id: string` (verificato W1 stub +\nisolation-module + permissions-module pattern). Test adjustato a `expect(mod.id).toBe(''fallbacks'')`.\nDocumentato in JSDoc test file header.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2d89f6242d3557c18ac3a19e0a4873581ef5bd72","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omardimarzio/GlueZero/git/trees/2d89f6242d3557c18ac3a19e0a4873581ef5bd72"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/omardimarzio/GlueZero/git/commits/d54db16067f1686d4d1ddf547a90f466a9777b94","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/406036?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/omardimarzio/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/