20e083def6ab02fd78492e1f5fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/ddf67c0bf04fc20e083def6ab02fd78492e1f5fb"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/71ae1dcbff6f3c4f5710da82e6fca4c2bd0b8304","sha":"71ae1dcbff6f3c4f5710da82e6fca4c2bd0b8304","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/71ae1dcbff6f3c4f5710da82e6fca4c2bd0b8304"}],"sha":"cc6bc5bccb605825a888b3436fef2df7753c3911","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/cc6bc5bccb605825a888b3436fef2df7753c3911"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/71ae1dcbff6f3c4f5710da82e6fca4c2bd0b8304/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:43:26Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T16:43:26Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"message":"fix(vr): wire the finalize spine, verifier gate, and confidence clamp\n\nA static sweep of the VR-truth change set found four capabilities whose\ncode was correct but whose production call-path was broken, plus a\nconfidence-gate gap. Each feature now runs.\n\n- Finalize aggregation spine: the aggregate step called\n  finalize_investigation_aggregate without the required outcome_model,\n  so it raised and the error was swallowed by the emit terminal''s guard.\n  Claim merge, branch promotion, the falsifier pass, and settled-claim\n  markers never ran. The emit bindings now carry the outcome model,\n  branch pool, falsifier, and ledger, and the seam threads them through.\n  The finalize pass also reaps stale open ledger requests\n  (contract_net.reap_stale_requests) and records per-persona\n  shared-claim coverage (shared_claims.read_shared_claims). The\n  LLM-oracle adjudicator had no caller at any tick and was removed\n  rather than shipped as a null wrapper.\n\n- Pre-dispatch verifier gate: the dispatcher imported verify_evidence\n  as a module attribute, but it existed only as an instance method, so\n  the import failed and verification was skipped for every positive\n  dispatch. A module-level verify_evidence entrypoint now instantiates\n  the verifier from the packet and delegates. The evidence packet\n  carries claim and index_id; when the payload omits index_id the vr\n  wrapper resolves it from the investigation target handles, keeping the\n  db_models lookup inside the vr module so the platform base never\n  imports vr internals.\n\n- Prompt-prefix caching default: the platform schema defaulted the flag\n  off, which the resolver read as an explicit operator kill switch, so a\n  base install never got the cheaper immutable-prefix layout the\n  resolver documents as the default. The schema default now matches.\n\n- broaden_promote_kinds flag: the flag was defined but never read; the\n  auto-promote source-kind check hardcoded the narrow default. The\n  check now resolves the flag and widens to any positive or inconclusive\n  outcome when enabled, preserving the narrow behavior when disabled or\n  on a config read fault.\n\n- Confidence gate clamp: a low self-report that resampled to high\n  through consensus bypassed the corroboration ceiling and could\n  auto-accept. The clamp is now centralized in the consensus pass and\n  applies to every consensus outcome, so an uncorroborated high can\n  never auto-accept on self-report alone.\n\nVerified: compileall, ruff, honesty audit (exit 0), and the outcome\ndispatcher, claim verifier, and gate suites pass.","tree":{"sha":"9c0922a951e74c65572e3507e60c9748b6ea3164","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/trees/9c0922a951e74c65572e3507e60c9748b6ea3164"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/commits/71ae1dcbff6f3c4f5710da82e6fca4c2bd0b8304","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/71ae1dcbff6f3c4f5710da82e6fca4c2bd0b8304","node_id":"C_kwDOSRC_-9oAKDcxYWUxZGNiZmY2ZjNjNGY1NzEwZGE4MmU2ZmNhNGMyYmQwYjgzMDQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/324d187dbee5d6733da27a6b898a9289bbac3bbf","sha":"324d187dbee5d6733da27a6b898a9289bbac3bbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/324d187dbee5d6733da27a6b898a9289bbac3bbf"}],"sha":"71ae1dcbff6f3c4f5710da82e6fca4c2bd0b8304","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/71ae1dcbff6f3c4f5710da82e6fca4c2bd0b8304"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/324d187dbee5d6733da27a6b898a9289bbac3bbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T14:32:47Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T14:32:47Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"message":"feat(vr): implement the deferred and partial VR-truth fixes\n\nLand the remaining VR-truth analysis-document fixes as one integrated\nchange set, folded under the unreleased 0.5.51 release. The prior\nconfirmation-wiring commit shipped part of the belief-write path; this\ncompletes it and adds the adjudication ledger, verifier evidence\npacket, tool-honesty floor, aggregation spine, and the confidence-gate\nre-sample inversion.\n\nLedger and knowledge:\n- Record reject/refute verdicts as a first-class `adjudication` ledger\n  kind so sibling branches read a dead lead instead of re-exploring it.\n- Consolidation ingests adjudication verdicts alongside discoveries and\n  notes, distilling negative knowledge.\n- Promote a confirmed finding into the verified pattern retrieval pool\n  on dispatch so the next hunt on the same target retrieves it.\n- Render discovery and adjudication board entries with a wider window\n  so a sibling sees the full claim, not a truncated stub. Remove the\n  note-coercion duplicate that inverted the phase-keyed coercion already\n  owned by turn_runner._post_ledger_writes.\n\nVerifier and belief:\n- Build the verifier evidence packet from branch case state and recorded\n  tool-call telemetry; widen the verifier trigger; add a pre-dispatch\n  binding gate; reject a positive submit whose citation is absent from\n  the telemetry.\n- Require a confirmation provenance and evidence references on a positive\n  submit; add a per-turn kill-criterion evaluator and a pre-draft\n  contradiction gate; surface `confirmed_by` in the hypothesis\n  projection and endpoint.\n- Wire the F1 promotion consumer omitted from the prior commit so a\n  confirmed hypothesis is acted on, and retract a refuted outcome\n  (superseded + rejected) so a downstream dispatcher cannot ship a claim\n  the run''s own adjudicator killed.\n\nTools:\n- Report an honest not-found result with the resolving file:line\n  coordinate instead of an indexer header; normalize tool namespaces at\n  the parse boundary; enforce search-before-read and a minimum tool-work\n  floor before dispatch.\n\nAggregation:\n- Add a shared claim space with owner-branch routing, a contract-net TTL\n  and reaper, a falsifier persona, and an investigation-level finalize\n  aggregation that merges duplicate-signature branch pairs, promotes the\n  strongest surviving positive, and writes settled-claim markers.\n\nConfidence gate:\n- Invert the re-sample target: the uncorroborated overconfident tail is\n  re-drawn for a second opinion and cannot be lifted back to high on a\n  repeated self-report; the honest low-confidence tail is no longer\n  re-drawn. Enable prompt-layout ordering by default for prompt caching.\n\nDistinctness:\n- Score a proposed finding against the seed and known corpus so a\n  restated known issue is not promoted as novel.\n\nGates: compileall, ruff, and honesty audit clean; targeted unit tests\ngreen across the ledger, verifier, gate, consolidator, aggregation, and\nsubmit-gate suites.","tree":{"sha":"f2605c0113030871bef7af5ab17f8ee3292047ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/trees/f2605c0113030871bef7af5ab17f8ee3292047ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/commits/324d187dbee5d6733da27a6b898a9289bbac3bbf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/324d187dbee5d6733da27a6b898a9289bbac3bbf","node_id":"C_kwDOSRC_-9oAKDMyNGQxODdkYmVlNWQ2NzMzZGEyN2E2Yjg5OGE5Mjg5YmJhYzNiYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/b9f1a873fadb82c04bd3e3f455c05139f0eb4209","sha":"b9f1a873fadb82c04bd3e3f455c05139f0eb4209","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/b9f1a873fadb82c04bd3e3f455c05139f0eb4209"}],"sha":"324d187dbee5d6733da27a6b898a9289bbac3bbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/324d187dbee5d6733da27a6b898a9289bbac3bbf"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/b9f1a873fadb82c04bd3e3f455c05139f0eb4209/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T13:34:10Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T13:34:10Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"message":"fix(vr): wire the F1 promotion consumer omitted from 8b11f6fb\n\nThe base promotion hooks (_inject_promotion_directives,\n_maybe_reject_weak_submit_with_confirmed_hypothesis), the\npromote_confirmed_findings config field, and the A2/A3 confirmed_by\nbelief-writes shipped in 8b11f6fb, but the sole consumer that reads the\nflag and implements the hooks was left uncommitted, leaving confirmed\nfindings recorded but never promoted.\n\nLand the HonestVulnResearcher override: read promote_confirmed_findings\nat configure time, inject a promote-the-confirmed-finding directive when\na live hypothesis carries confirmed_by, and block a weak-polarity submit\n(audit_memo / assessment_report) that would bury a confirmed hypothesis,\nforcing a direct_finding or an explicit retraction. Purely additive.","tree":{"sha":"8cff8a4e8ce7e6e787315283563d179637613fd4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/trees/8cff8a4e8ce7e6e787315283563d179637613fd4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/commits/b9f1a873fadb82c04bd3e3f455c05139f0eb4209","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/b9f1a873fadb82c04bd3e3f455c05139f0eb4209","node_id":"C_kwDOSRC_-9oAKGI5ZjFhODczZmFkYjgyYzA0YmQzZTNmNDU1YzA1MTM5ZjBlYjQyMDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/8b11f6fb3ead79b9fe0d85cb1223d39d5eed9d95","sha":"8b11f6fb3ead79b9fe0d85cb1223d39d5eed9d95","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/8b11f6fb3ead79b9fe0d85cb1223d39d5eed9d95"}],"sha":"b9f1a873fadb82c04bd3e3f455c05139f0eb4209","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/b9f1a873fadb82c04bd3e3f455c05139f0eb4209"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/8b11f6fb3ead79b9fe0d85cb1223d39d5eed9d95/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:33:27Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-30T12:33:27Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"message":"feat(vr): wire confirmation into belief and reach the verifier\n\nLand the consolidated VR distinctive-truth work for release 0.5.51.\n\n- Belief: a quorum-approved outcome and a taint-confirmed discovery\n  record confirmation provenance on the originating hypothesis, so a\n  confirmed belief reaches the branch state the engine reasons from;\n  confirmed-finding promotion is enabled by default.\n- Verifier: auto-promotion fires for any dispatched confirmed finding\n  above the confidence floor, not only an operator-skipped dead-end; the\n  extractor and verdict run through schema-validated structured output\n  instead of free-text parsing that defaulted to inconclusive.\n- Reach-emit: a run that exhausts its turn budget without an outcome\n  stays resumable with one reserved emit-and-verify attempt; a terminal\n  investigation drives a stranded workflow cursor to a terminal sentinel.\n- Knowledge: consolidation ingests confirmed discoveries only, semantic\n  and pattern knowledge is tiered verified only with a confirmation\n  marker, and the pruner evicts refuted or superseded entries.\n- Gate: a high self-reported confidence no longer auto-accepts without a\n  corroborating signal.\n- Cost documentation corrected to the on-write plus live-recompute\n  design; the cost value is written, not decorative.\n\nNo schema migration; confirmation state rides existing JSON. Platform\nbases keep backward-compatible signatures for the malware and forensics\nmodules. Part of the vr-truth issue set (#247-#273), closed via PR #244.","tree":{"sha":"784fd3063429da1539c748fc0ecfccc44006a088","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/trees/784fd3063429da1539c748fc0ecfccc44006a088"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/commits/8b11f6fb3ead79b9fe0d85cb1223d39d5eed9d95","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","