pos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/4bf90af24692ea22664e130200a9dd529698deec/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:05:59Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T01:05:59Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"message":"fix(workflow): wire module_id in vr and malware setup bindings\n\nSpecialist agents resolving to a capability and routing to dedicated lane phases requires module_id to be populated in the state setup bindings. Previously, vr and malware setup bindings omitted module_id, which caused branch capabilities to resolve to None and skipped all capability-scoped phases. Specifying the module identifier enables capability resolution for specialist personas and corrects the corresponding inline comments and registry test assertions.","tree":{"sha":"d16c6b8ce619d413cae433be139602f5991c696e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/trees/d16c6b8ce619d413cae433be139602f5991c696e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/commits/4bf90af24692ea22664e130200a9dd529698deec","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/4bf90af24692ea22664e130200a9dd529698deec","node_id":"C_kwDOSRC_-9oAKDRiZjkwYWYyNDY5MmVhMjI2NjRlMTMwMjAwYTlkZDUyOTY5OGRlZWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/03254cd1622f666f65570cd5652bc61b95cfc7cc","sha":"03254cd1622f666f65570cd5652bc61b95cfc7cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/03254cd1622f666f65570cd5652bc61b95cfc7cc"}],"sha":"4bf90af24692ea22664e130200a9dd529698deec","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/4bf90af24692ea22664e130200a9dd529698deec"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/03254cd1622f666f65570cd5652bc61b95cfc7cc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:59:04Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:59:04Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"message":"fix(console): resolve llm-log blank envelope row rendering\n\nThe list endpoint returns an envelope object containing metadata and a nested data payload. When offset pagination is enabled, the client fetches the full envelope. The utility mapping function did not descend into the nested data field when it was a non-array object, causing the grid to render the top-level envelope itself as a single blank row. Descending into the nested object correctly extracts the array of records, restoring pagination alignment.","tree":{"sha":"6c39bd6ef642b28141e8b3fd9b8a129c71addc9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/trees/6c39bd6ef642b28141e8b3fd9b8a129c71addc9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/commits/03254cd1622f666f65570cd5652bc61b95cfc7cc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/03254cd1622f666f65570cd5652bc61b95cfc7cc","node_id":"C_kwDOSRC_-9oAKDAzMjU0Y2QxNjIyZjY2NmY2NTU3MGNkNTY1MmJjNjFiOTVjZmM3Y2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commit/c00c87ffd5bf6cc829dbf110968781eff20b3b71","sha":"c00c87ffd5bf6cc829dbf110968781eff20b3b71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/c00c87ffd5bf6cc829dbf110968781eff20b3b71"}],"sha":"03254cd1622f666f65570cd5652bc61b95cfc7cc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/03254cd1622f666f65570cd5652bc61b95cfc7cc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/c00c87ffd5bf6cc829dbf110968781eff20b3b71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:55:40Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-26T00:55:40Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"message":"fix(notifications): surface __system__ producer rows in reads\n\nThe cost.py missing-pricing and budget_alert.py 80%/100% producers write\nNotificationRecord rows with user_id=\"__system__\", but every read endpoint\nscoped to auth.user_id, so those alerts were unreachable from the console\ncenter. list_notifications and get_unread_notifications now union the\ncaller''s rows with __system__ rows, making the alerts visible to any\nauthenticated user. The three mutation endpoints keep the ownership check,\nso system rows stay read-only (mark-read, read-all, and delete reject them\nwith 404); real user rows remain private to their owner.\n\nVerified: 7/7 notification tests pass against aila_test (2 new tests cover\nsystem-row visibility to any user and the read-only 404s), compileall,\nruff, and the honesty audit are clean.","tree":{"sha":"796dc8826944a76887d86f1692f53e0c64351fbd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/trees/796dc8826944a76887d86f1692f53e0c64351fbd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/commits/c00c87ffd5bf6cc829dbf110968781eff20b3b71","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/echel0nn","id":16112212,"login":"echel0nn","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTEyMjEy","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/orgs","r