received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/commits/7072a24239bf62f90c8e71547c636094e6d3f103/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T19:36:37Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T19:36:37Z","email":"melih.sahin@protonmail.com","name":"echel0nn"},"message":"feat(console): surface finding workflow state on vr:findings list\n\nThe vr module already declares its finding lifecycle extension\n(vr.false_positive, vr.accepted_risk) and /vr/findings rows carry a\npopulated workflow_state, but the vr:findings list rendered neither the\nstate nor any transition control, leaving VR''s own findings surface\nunable to advance the lifecycle the backend enforces. Adds a\nWorkflowStateBadge column, a state select filter, and the legal-edge\ntransition actions, mirroring the malware:findings block so both module\nfindings views read and move state the same way.","tree":{"sha":"e8290b4d232bec61cd724c0429873b15ef1ddbd0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/trees/e8290b4d232bec61cd724c0429873b15ef1ddbd0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/project-lambda-zero/AILA/git/commits/7072a24239bf62f90c8e71547c636094e6d3f103","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16112212?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/echel0nn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"http